  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Cultivating Talent on the North Coast of Honduras</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The north coast of Honduras has a high rate of violence and migration. With few alternatives for employment, youth living in peri-urban areas are susceptible to influences of organized crime in nearby cities and along major transit routes. ESMAG-El Pinowill work with children, youth and adults in approximately 10 communitiesof the municipality of El Porvenir in the biological corridor between the Pico Bonito National Park (PNPB) and the Cuero y Salado Wildlife Refuge (RVSCS) on the north coast of Honduras. ESMAG-El Pino will promote leadership andentrepreneurshipskills and build environmental awareness through an Ethics School, ecotourism, community development activities, reforestation and small business development.ESMAG-El Pino will increase its own revenue through product development and marketing.The project will directly benefit 675 individuals and indirectly benefit approximately 10,000 individuals.</narrative>
  </description>
